
  Welcome to the GeSI Gentoo installer — the HeDE desktop.

  The image boots into HeDE (the Helm Desktop Environment). Open GeST from the
  ≡ Apps menu (or run `gest` in a terminal) and choose "Install Gentoo" to
  partition a disk, unpack a stage3, and install Gentoo — the Handbook, driven
  by GeST, with a real desktop, terminal, and file manager available while you
  work.

  If you land on this console instead of the desktop, the HeDE session failed
  to start — run `gest` here to install from the TUI.

  Networking: a wired link usually comes up via DHCP automatically. For Wi-Fi,
  use the panel's network indicator, GeST → Network → Wi-Fi, or
  `wpa_supplicant`/`iw` by hand before installing (the install downloads a
  stage3 and emerges packages).
